# saphira-router control-plane identity.
#
# The core needs NO privileged socket and NO hardware access, so it does not
# run as root (D1 section 8). Anything genuinely privileged is performed at a
# helper/drone boundary on the managed host, never here.
#
# UID/GID namespace: 0..199 preferred, 888..999 forbidden, 1000+ human.
#
# 151 is allocated in package-name order from 147, the first free ID above the
# highest claimed identity (146 openldap), clear of hatchling's systemd block
# (127-131, 144, 145). The choice is verified against BOTH acceptance hosts,
# not one: 127 is free on egg but is systemd-network on hatchling.
#
# It is NOT the 132 this fragment previously declared. 132 avoided systemd's
# block but collided with qmail, which is published - a package the earlier
# check did not consult. saphira-router is unpublished and disabled, so the
# move costs no migration and needs no legacy sidecar.
group saphira-router 151
user saphira-router 151 saphira-router /var/lib/saphira-router /sbin/nologin
dir  /var/lib/saphira-router 0750 saphira-router saphira-router
dir  /run/saphira-router 0755 saphira-router saphira-router
